course: dictionary
lesson: 11451
title: Formal words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Adjudge is a formal word. It means to decide officially, the way a judge or referee does. When someone is adjudged something, an official has made a judgement about them or about something.
explain: Look at the clues around it. «The ball was adjudged to have crossed the line.» A referee makes an official decision, so the sentence tells you the referee decided the ball crossed the line. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The ball was decided to have crossed the line" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: The word is often used with was or were: «The runner was adjudged the winner.» «The driver was adjudged guilty.» The word shows that an official made the decision, not just that someone thought so.
fact: Adjudge means to decide officially that something is true, or that someone is something.
fact: In a court case, to adjudge means to give an official decision.
fact: «Adjudged» is the past form, as in «The team was adjudged the winner.»
fact: Referees adjudge things in sport, such as whether a goal counts, a foul was made, or a player was offside.
fact: Adjudge is a formal word, so you will meet it most in sports reports, law and official writing.
exercise: «The goal was adjudged offside.» What does adjudged mean here? | Seen by the fans | *Officially decided | Forgotten | Kicked very hard
exercise: The judge adjudged the man guilty. What did the judge do? | Let him go home for lunch | *Made an official decision that he was guilty | Bought him a drink | Said sorry to him
exercise: Find and copy the word in this sentence that is a form of adjudge: «The team was adjudged the winner.» | *adjudged | was | winner | team
test: «The referee adjudged that the player had fouled.» Who made the official decision? | The fans | *The referee | The coach | The player
test: Which word is closest in meaning to adjudge? | Whisper | Stretch | *Decide officially | Forget
exam: «The judges adjudged the cake the winner of the show.» What does adjudged mean? | *Officially decided | Ate | Lost | Baked
